From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruiyangke <me@ry.ke>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:04:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gpui: Pin the terminal keyboard snapshot

Pin the six gpui-pre 0.3.9 crates to ruiyangke/gpui-kit@ab40fa8 (branch
codex/gpui-terminal-snapshot). That snapshot is the same Zed revision as
gpui-pre 0.3.9 (93d7456), built with upstream's snapshot generator, plus
terminal-keyboard.patch.

The patch adds an optional physical key and native layout metadata (original
key text, raw modifiers, lock states) to KeyDownEvent and KeyUpEvent, and
Window::numlock(). Newport's terminal needs them to encode keys the way a
terminal expects; GPUI's shortcut-oriented Keystroke drops them. Synthetic
events leave the fields empty, so shortcut dispatch is unchanged. Kit's event
constructors initialize the new fields; the gpui-fast backend is untouched.

Remove when GPUI exposes physical keys and layout metadata on key events.
